node_modules/
dist/

# Generated artifacts, named one by one rather than as a bare `*.html`.
#
# The bare pattern silently ignored every HTML file anywhere in the repo, including
# ones nobody meant to ignore — `examples/report/index.html` was being dropped by it
# without anyone deciding that. A rule that swallows files you never named is the git
# spelling of `2>/dev/null`. [LAW:no-silent-failure]
#
# Both files below regenerate in about a second from checked-in inputs, and both are
# large enough (300 KB and 1.3 MB) that committing them would dwarf the source they
# come from. The screenshots in examples/hand-trace/screenshots/ are the durable
# record; the HTML is not.
examples/hand-trace/flamegraph.html
examples/report/index.html
examples/report/corpus.json

# Chrome profiles are managed by `crom`, never checked in.
examples/**/.chrome-profile/
# Diagnostic screenshots from a failed verify run are transient.
examples/**/screenshots/FAILED-*.png
